      "text": "At a planning meeting, Maya presents a proposal for a book swap that thirty students will attend. “We recommend using the library meeting room because it will keep the books dry.” “According to the current notice, the room is available on Friday.” “The main advantage is that we won't need to cancel if it rains.” Ben adds, “However, there's a limit of twenty people, so we suggest two sessions of fifteen.” A classmate asks how they will keep the reading area quiet. “We could close the meeting-room door and ask everyone to keep their voices down,” Maya replies. “Our next step is to ask the librarian to reserve the room,” Maya says, and the group agrees.",
